# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual API keys.
# Never commit .env to version control.

# ── LLM (agents) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider: anthropic (default) | openai | gemini | ollama | ollama-cloud
LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# Model id. Defaults per provider: claude-sonnet-4-6 / gpt-4o /
# gemini-1.5-pro / llama3.1:8b. Override to use a different model.
LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# ── Embeddings (FAISS index + RAG query) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Provider: ollama (default, local, free) | openai
# IMPORTANT: build_index.py and rag_tool.py must use the same provider/model,
# or FAISS retrieval returns garbage. Both import from chatbot/embeddings.py.
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=ollama
OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=mxbai-embed-large
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OPENAI_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# OLLAMA_LLM_BASE_URL (optional, unset by default): overrides OLLAMA_BASE_URL
# for the LOCAL "ollama" provider's generation only, e.g. to point at a
# different local/LAN Ollama server while embeddings stay on the one above.
# For Ollama CLOUD, use LLM_PROVIDER=ollama-cloud below instead — that's a
# separate first-class lane, not an override on this one.

# ── Ollama Cloud (LLM_PROVIDER=ollama-cloud — dev/iteration lane) ────────────
# A capable hosted model with more daily headroom than Gemini's free tier,
# for cheaply tuning the generation pipeline — NOT a substitute for the
# paper's final Sonnet pass. Set:
#   LLM_PROVIDER=ollama-cloud
#   LLM_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b        (confirmed present via GET /v1/models)
#   OLLAMA_API_KEY=<your Ollama Cloud API key, id.secret format from
#                    ollama.com/settings/keys>
# This is the regular-API-key-as-bearer-token path against Ollama Cloud's
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint (confirmed live: HTTP 200 on GET /v1/models
# and on a real /v1/chat/completions call) — NOT `ollama signin`/the
# ssh-ed25519 device-key flow, which is a different auth mechanism for a
# locally-run `ollama serve` proxying to the cloud and 401s if you paste a
# regular API key into it expecting it to work the same way.
#
# llm.py's ollama-cloud branch passes api_key= explicitly to CrewAI's
# OpenAICompatibleCompletion (not litellm — this CrewAI version doesn't
# route Ollama/Gemini/Anthropic through litellm at all, confirmed by grep;
# "litellm num_retries" or similar has no effect here). Optional
# OLLAMA_CLOUD_BASE_URL overrides the default https://ollama.com if ever
# needed (rarely).
#
# This var is SEPARATE from OLLAMA_BASE_URL above (embeddings + the plain
# local "ollama" provider) — embeddings.py never reads OLLAMA_API_KEY or
# OLLAMA_CLOUD_BASE_URL, so embeddings always stay local regardless. It's
# also SAFE to leave OLLAMA_API_KEY set even when LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# (local): that branch now explicitly passes api_key="ollama" (Ollama's
# own documented no-auth-needed dummy value) so it can never fall back to
# reading this var — without that fix, a live OLLAMA_API_KEY here would
# silently attach a Bearer header to local calls too, which per
# docs.ollama.com/api/authentication can 403 a local server that doesn't
# expect any Authorization header at all.
OLLAMA_CLOUD_BASE_URL=
OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# ── Ollama context window (only relevant when LLM_PROVIDER=ollama) ───────────
# Ollama's own default (4096) can silently truncate long prompts. This
# project's agent backstories + injected RAG content can get long, so a
# larger context window is recommended. HOWEVER: this is NOT a variable to
# set in this .env file — chatbot/llm.py deliberately does not pass num_ctx
# to crewai.LLM() for Ollama models, after it broke crew.kickoff() twice
# with `TypeError: Completions.create() got an unexpected keyword argument
# 'num_ctx'` (a CrewAI-internal-routing issue — see CLAUDE.md, "Ollama
# Context Window", for the full history).
#
# Set it on the Ollama SERVER process instead, e.g.:
#   OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=8192 ollama serve
# Or, if Ollama runs as the macOS menu-bar app (not a manually-run `ollama
# serve`):
#   launchctl setenv OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH 8192
#   (then restart the Ollama app)
# Confirmed real Ollama env var per https://docs.ollama.com/faq ("How can I
# specify the context window size?"). Not yet live-confirmed by this
# project that raising it actually reduces crash rates — the original
# truncation hypothesis is still unverified.
